sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch08-01> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "For a rectangular cell to be divided equally by a partition of least area, the partition must cut across its longest axis, and in successive bisections each new partition must be at right angles to the one before.";
    dc:type "mathematical-law";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Minimal bisecting walls cut the longest axis and alternate at right angles";
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "minimal bisecting partition of a rectangular cell \\perp longest axis; successive partitions mutually \\perp";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter VIII, “The Forms of Tissues, or Cell-Aggregates (continued)”; topic “Minimal partitions in rectangular cells”. Scope: dividing cells of roughly rectangular shape, especially in plant tissues"
}
